{"title":"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/7/86705e4060f3b52a640371be86bdaf1806453078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^1(x)=(x-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"21\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/668362e3bbcc4c71ca10863a4cdb9430b789660e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^n(x)=f^1(f^{n-1}(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a70f9a72d15f037c2a12d5e57575e0e22bf5f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f^7(2)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square with side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units is rotated around one of its sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. The volume the square sweeps out can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c7913ad7683d80ca363fb9ba6ad07033c340cc2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\pi$\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66cdd25e10195f4c5170cb0f6173522f08afff8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a@b=\\frac{a^2-b^2}{a+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"116\" height=\"42\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/5496a82ad1ba4dd9d9bbde30e32a0c0f7c5acdd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1@(2@(\\dots(2020@2021)\\dots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is placed inside of a right isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0526e1f5ad1412706cf938657f754604e672a671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/83756d2811fdd31447c86df5261bd59ab9a111ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XYZ=90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb2419be49ff83cbed7db9a2f366858ccabf2e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XZ$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0526e1f5ad1412706cf938657f754604e672a671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of ways to arrange the characters in \"delicious greenbeans\" into two separate strings of letters can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/affce65eff17cf2a28041ed32c710dfc05840f28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot b!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is maximized and both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. (A string of letters is defined as a group of consecutive letters with no spaces between them.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bag weighs 1 pound and can hold 16 pounds of food at maximum. Danny buys 100 packages of tomatoes and 300 packages of potatoes. Tomatoes come in packages that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces each and potatoes come in packages that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces each. All of Danny’s food must be packed into bags, and Danny will use only as many bags as he needs. What is the minimum possible weight, in pounds, of Danny’s luggage, including the bags?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bffde82eacf9a3adb183dd3b16141711d10977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=13,AC=14,BC=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" /> and incircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. A second circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is drawn which is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/5/e956bb95054645df67798a7d96dbb4556f129920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> and externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. The radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a5bf6feb2cf6debc24e4aac8c9115957b87115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a-b\\sqrt{c}}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a squarefree positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a643bcc8195884f4fc1e16966f6f3d6ad6fe2c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947add5766b9f26f6dfe73d9425d87664416459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of ways to seat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> distinguishable people around a hexagon with two people seated on each side, where the order of the two people on each side does not matter and rotations are disregarded. Find the number of divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nBobby is going to throw 20 darts at the dartboard shown below. It is formed by 4 concentric circles, with radii of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/97827a34a0f6699ae2b5fd23665cc8eecd056286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, with the largest circle being inscribed in a square. Each point on the dartboard has an equally likely chance of being hit by a dart, and Bobby is guaranteed to hit the dartboard. Each region is labeled with its point value (the number of points Bobby will get if he hits that region). The expected number of points Bobby will get after throwing the 20 darts can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43e8a8e8711c11f71a1c61eb0f57063b4cc4c2b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. </p><center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa99ca5c6ecf34b940029025c5aee1edd26e0b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm);  filldraw(shift(-7,-7)*((0,0)--(14,0)--(14,14)--(0,14)--cycle),gray);  filldraw(circle((0,0),7),white); filldraw(circle((0,0),5),white); filldraw(circle((0,0),3),white); filldraw(circle((0,0),1),white);  label(&quot;$70$&quot;,(0,0)); label(&quot;$-28$&quot;,(0,2)); label(&quot;$49$&quot;,(0,4)); label(&quot;$-21$&quot;,(0,6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(-6,6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(6,6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(-6,-6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(6,-6)); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"238\" /> </center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d8450081396c663a3c6aab461e8df32c185bf83c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underbrace{2021^{2022^{\\ldots^{2022^{2021}}}}}_{2021\\text{ } 2021\\text{&#39;}s}\\cdot\\underbrace{2022^{2021^{\\ldots^{2021^{2022}}}}}_{2022\\text{ }2022\\text{&#39;}s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"258\" height=\"51\" /> is divided by 11.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017131529\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 286/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9225/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22383:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017131529 and revision id 274568. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}